| `TASK-260720-9xy8yx` | PacketFlow adapter callback/cancellation lifecycle hardening | `validation.md` cancellation/start-stop rows and `packet-plane.md` bounded lifecycle work. |
| `TASK-260715-2jatnd` | One binding M0 gate/configuration/fork decision | `delivery.md` M0 exit and `validation.md` M0 Bridge gate. |
| `BUG-260720-2zh86a` | Normalize pinned HEV and ReluxLibSSH2 XCFramework deployment metadata in the deterministic vendor build path | Justified gap: ADR-016 and `validation.md` require iOS 18/macOS 15 slices and a passing Apple native matrix, but the spec did not define how to repair pinned artifacts whose slices advertised older deployment targets. Before creation, scope checks excluded upstream C patches, MTU/framing, routes, DNS, SSH protocol behavior, and relay changes; the fix remained build/vendor-path only. `BUG-260720-2zh86a_results.md` and accepted `BUG-260720-2zh86a_review.md` provide the concrete evidence. |
| `BUG-260720-2p4fln` | Preserve traffic statistics across teardown | Justified gap: the literal spec requires counters and clean lifecycle but did not define capture ordering. Out-of-scope checks confirmed no HEV pin, framing, route, DNS, SSH, or relay change. |
| `BUG-260720-24f9w6` | Remove a coverage-instrumentation timing false signal | Justified gap: deterministic gate evidence is required, but the spec does not prescribe the test-observation mechanism. Out-of-scope checks confirmed no production behavior or threshold change. |

The accepted physical evidence is deliberately owned outside this implementation
Story by `TASK-260715-gyg51r` and `TASK-260715-135rr8`; duplicating those manual
gate tasks here would weaken provenance. No new research task or diagram is
needed for this synthesis.

